WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.020
Rhiannon: Children and young people
may need help with a wide range of

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.060
issues at different points in their
lives, and parents and carers may

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:12.459
also need help and advice to deal with
behavioural or other mental health

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.459
problems their child is experiencing.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:19.750
For those experiencing mental health
problems GPs are often a starting

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.350
point, and they can give advice or refer
children and young people to counsellors

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.529
and therapists who will be able to
give more specialist assistance whether

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.660
this is through the NHS or privately.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.069
Counsellors and therapists can also
be approached directly and there are

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.340
many organisations online that can
recommend or showcase these services.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.730
Children and Young People’s Mental
Health Services or CAMHS as they

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.679
maybe referred to, cover all services
that work with children and young

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:54.710
people who have difficulties with
their mental health or wellbeing.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.810
They include psychiatrists and
psychologists and primary health

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.370
care workers and specialists.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.220
A referral to CAMHS for an assessment can
be via a parent or carer, the individual

00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:11.350
if they are old enough, a GP or teacher,
or via a school or social service.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.580
Getting help from a specialist
CAMHS is different dependent on

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.960
area and waiting times can vary.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.240
Youngminds.org.uk is committed
to improving the emotional

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.030
well-being and mental health
of children and young people.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.729
They campaign, research and aim to
influence policy and practice based on the

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:35.150
experiences of children and young people
they work with, as well as their families

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.469
and the professionals who support them,
to help them to develop better well-being.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:45.209
Mind.org.uk is perhaps the most
well-known of all mental health charities.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.809
Mind’s aim is to provide advice
and support to empower anyone

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.899
experiencing a mental health problem.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.360
They campaign to improve services, raise
awareness and promote understanding

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.233
and offer specific information and
support for young people aged 11 to 18

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.919
who are going through a difficult time.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.420
They also offer supported housing,
drop-in centres, crisis helplines,

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.980
talking therapies, employment
and training schemes, counselling

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.280
and befriending services.

00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:24.299
Stem4.org.uk is a charity that
promotes positive mental health

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.040
in teenagers and those who support
them including their families and

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.500
carers, education professionals,
as well as school nurses and GPs.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.760
through the provision of mental
health education, resilience

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.999
strategies and early intervention.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.786
This is initially through the provision
of mental health education, resilience

00:02:39.786 --> 00:02:41.299
strategies and early intervention,
provided digitally, through their website.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.620
There are many other charities and
local initiatives involved in supporting

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.250
good mental well-being, and role of the
voluntary and community organisations

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.529
in supporting mental health issues,
plays a very important role and they

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.170
sit outside of clinical settings.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.959
Some local areas may also provide
drop-in sessions or support groups

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.530
run by volunteers, where children
and young people can get together.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.010
The good thing about the support
framework within the charity and volunteer

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.309
sector, for those with mental health
problems, are that they can influence and

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:15.490
participate in projects or activities.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.049
Helping them to increased levels of
confidence and boost their self-esteem

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:26.970
also helping their mental well-being.

